# OS / editor
.DS_Store

# Node
node_modules
dist/

# Scaffolding: design drafts, research, sprint notes. Working material, not the product.
# The decisions they produced live in .wst/memory/decisions/ — that is what travels.
_design/

# Whetstone: memory index is a regenerable cache (M2 SQLite adapter).
# Files under .wst/memory/ remain the source of truth and ARE committed.
.wst/memory/index.db

# Compiled check index: regenerable from .wst/checks/*.md via `wst check --compile`.
# Deliberately NOT committed — a compiled artifact that can silently go stale is the
# same trap as trusting a version string for identity.
.wst/checks/_index.json

# Agent worktrees created by the harness. Embedded git repositories, so a `git add -A`
# sweeps them into a commit as gitlinks — which is what happened on 2026-08-12 before
# someone caught it. `git worktree remove` is how they go, not `rm`.
.claude/worktrees/

# Per-worktree lane marker, read by .claude/hooks/lane-guard.mjs. Belongs to the
# worktree, not to the branch — committing it would scope every clone to one lane.
.wst-lane

# The briefing `wst run --prepare` writes into a leased worktree. Same argument as
# .wst-lane: it belongs to the worktree, not the branch. Observed — a crewmate ran
# `git add -A` and swept its own charter into the diff it was dispatched to produce.
.wst-charter.md

# The execution log: what a gate run did, minute by minute. NOT committed, and this
# is the one call in ADR-0011's first move the proposal did not cover — flagged on
# the PR rather than settled here.
#
# Two reasons. It is per-machine runtime state: `signals.jsonl` records judgments a
# team shares, this records that one laptop ran the gate at 14:02. And committing it
# closes a loop — the pre-push hook runs the gate, the gate writes this file, the
# tree is dirty after the push, and the NEXT run sees a changed file to triage.
#
# What that costs: comparing two agents across machines needs a shared log. That is
# move 3, and it wants a real answer about retention, not a default set today.
.wst/events.jsonl

# Receipts are a derived cache: "check X passed on this exact input". Regenerable,
# and a stale one would claim a pass that never happened for the current code.
# Worse than stale if COMMITTED: a receipt authorises skipping a check, so every
# clone would inherit skips it never earned — one of them a paid LLM verdict.
.wst/receipts/
